{% include 'brand' %}
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">High-rise HVAC · GTA</p>
    <h1>{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ section.settings.lede }}</p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn-call" href="{{ sx_tel }}">Call {{ sx_phone }}</a>
      <a class="btn-outline" href="/pages/contact-residential-commercial-hvac-company-gta?job=condo&property=condo#job-request">Request a condo tech</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    {{ section.settings.body }}
  </div>
</section>
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Condo page",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "H1",
      "default": "Condo fan coils and water-source heat pumps — not generic “quality.”"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "lede",
      "label": "Lede",
      "default": "If the closet unit is blowing warm air or the pan is leaking into the suite below, you need a high-rise tech, not a furnace flyer. We work VFC, WSHP, Magic Pak, PTAC, and Sky Mark."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "<p>Most GTA towers do not use a basement furnace. Heat and cooling live in a vertical fan coil, a water-source heat pump, a Magic Pak through the wall, a PTAC, or a Sky Mark package. Those systems share building water or a condenser loop. A house tech who only carries furnace boards will stare at the closet and guess.</p><p>Tell us the make on the indoor label. We aim to diagnose in one visit. Same-day and one-trip language stays only if the owner still runs that policy — confirm before advertising it on ads.</p><p>After-hours condo calls are dispatch intent. We take the call; a truck is assigned when a technician is free. Management offices and unit owners can both book.</p>"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
